Package: nassie
Version: 0.1.33
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), python3-rich, python3-pyside6.qtcore, python3-pyside6.qtgui, python3-pyside6.qtwidgets, samba
Recommends: policykit-1, python3-qrcode
Maintainer: Caden Lister <cadenlister@gmail.com>
Description: NASsie - cross-platform SMB share configuration wizard
 A terminal-UI wizard by default ('nassie'), with a PySide6/Qt desktop UI
 available via 'nassie --gui-qt' (or the TUI's/basic CLI's own "Launch
 Desktop UI" entry), for creating and managing SMB (Samba) shares. Walks
 the user through share name, path, and user credentials, then applies
 the configuration on Linux by installing Samba if needed, writing the
 smb.conf share block, creating the system user, and restarting the
 Samba services.
 Requests root privileges via a native polkit (pkexec) prompt when
 not already run as root, falling back to a terminal sudo prompt.
